<h1>Flim Summaries — privacy</h1>
<p class="lede-inline">
  Draft privacy notice for the optional Flim Summaries service only. Not
  counsel-approved. Controller: Panu Hällfors —
  <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>.
</p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>
  We keep what the account needs (your email and plan state). We keep IP
  addresses for rate limiting and troubleshooting for <strong>30 days</strong>,
  not linked to message content. We do <strong>not</strong> keep voice audio,
  room context, transcripts, titles, or summaries after the request finishes.
</p>

<h2>What we store</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account email</strong> — so we can send sign-in codes and recognise your account. Kept while the account exists.</li>
  <li><strong>Session, plan, allowance, promo redemptions</strong> (and later store-purchase references if those ship) — kept while needed for the account.</li>
  <li><strong>IP addresses</strong> — for rate limiting and troubleshooting, retained about 30 days, not tied to message contents.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What we process but do not keep</h2>
<p>
  For each request the app may send voice audio and a little room context. We
  run speech-to-text and summarisation, return title, summary, and transcript to
  your phone, then discard that content. It is not stored for later browsing or
  training on our side.
</p>

<h2>Where</h2>
<p>
  Processing stays in the EU as far as this service is concerned: hosting and
  database on UpCloud in Finland; inference through Cortecs with EU-only
  routing.
</p>

<h2>Sub-processors</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>UpCloud</strong> — hosting and managed database (Finland).</li>
  <li><strong>Cortecs</strong> — EU-routed transcription and summary models.</li>
  <li><strong>Resend</strong> — sending sign-in emails.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>
  You can ask for access, correction, or deletion of account data, and lodge a
  complaint with a supervisory authority. Contact
  <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>.
  Deleting the account removes the stored account fields; IP logs age out on the
  30-day schedule.
</p>

